@*
    The Tasks page on the settings screen (settings/tasks), which the shell draws
    because the host registered it (AddTasksSettings) rather than because the shell
    knows anything about tasks. One card today, My Day, holding one switch: Clear
    My Day overnight (local ADR 0032; .devbook/domain/tasks/context.md#clear-my-day-overnight).

    The switch changes how a myday: stamp from an earlier day is read, and never
    writes one, so turning it back on restores the overnight list at once. It saves
    on change, through IMyDayPreferences, and the sync carries it to the person's
    other desktops and phone as one document.

    The namespace is the project's root rather than a Settings folder's, for the
    reason InboxSettings gives: a ...Tasks.Settings namespace would shadow the
    settings screen's own component.
*@
@namespace Backlog.Desktop.UI.Tasks
@using Backlog.UI.Components.Settings
@implements IDisposable
@inject IMyDayPreferences Preferences

<SettingsHeadline>@Headline(Preferences.ClearsOvernight)</SettingsHeadline>

@* In the grid every settings page lays its cards out in, so the one card keeps
   the grid's width cap rather than stretching across the page. *@
<div class="setting-columns">
<SettingsCard Title="@MyDayCardTitle"
              Id="tasks-my-day-title"
              Description="What happens overnight to the tasks you put in My Day. The choice travels to your other paired devices."
              TestId="tasks-my-day-card">
    <Toggle Label="Clear My Day overnight"
            Description="On, My Day starts empty every morning. Off, a task you have not finished stays in My Day until you finish it — without the time you had planned it for, which was that day's."
            Checked="@Preferences.ClearsOvernight"
            CheckedChanged="SetClearsOvernight"
            TestId="tasks-my-day-clears-overnight" />

    @* Said only when the value could not be written: the switch still moved, for
       this session, and the line says why it may not survive a restart. *@
    <Alert Message="@_error"
           Role="status"
           TestId="tasks-my-day-status" />
</SettingsCard>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The page's one card - what its <c>SettingsSection.CardTitles</c>
    /// declares.</summary>
    public const string MyDayCardTitle = "My Day";

    /// <summary>The cards the page draws, in order: what the settings search reads.</summary>
    public static IReadOnlyList<string> CardTitles { get; } = [MyDayCardTitle];

    /// <summary>The sentence the frame shows over this page: what My Day does
    /// overnight, under the switch as it stands.</summary>
    public static string Headline(bool clearsOvernight) => clearsOvernight
        ? "My Day starts empty every morning."
        : "My Day keeps what you have not finished until you finish it.";

    private string? _error;

    protected override void OnInitialized() => Preferences.Changed += OnPreferencesChanged;

    private void SetClearsOvernight(bool clearsOvernight) =>
        _error = Preferences.SetClearsOvernight(clearsOvernight);

    /// <summary>The switch moved somewhere else — another window, or a copy a sync
    /// pull took from another desktop — on whichever thread that happened.</summary>
    private void OnPreferencesChanged() => _ = InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);

    public void Dispose() => Preferences.Changed -= OnPreferencesChanged;
}
